<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>{{ t("chat.page.conversations-targum", "Conversations — targum") }}</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('reader.css') }}{{ asset('chrome.css') }}{{ asset('composer.css') }}{{ asset('chat.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{% if embed %}
{#- Framed in the front page (design.md §13, 2026-09-11): the chrome's face rides with
    the bar on every other page, and here there is no bar; every link opens in the
    page that holds the frame, never inside it. -#}
{{ chrome_face() }}
<base target="_top">
{% endif %}
<script>{{ asset('keep.js') }}</script>
</head>
<body class="chat{% if embed %} embed{% endif %}">
{% set here = 'chat' %}
{% if not embed %}
{% include '_nav.html.j2' %}
<script>{{ asset('building.js') }}</script>
{% endif %}
<main class="chat-main">
  {#- The conversations you have had, newest first, and one door to a fresh one. A
      hairline list rather than a raised panel: §9, one raised layer per view, and the
      thread is the one. -#}
  <aside class="chat-side">
    <div class="chat-side-head">
      <button type="button" id="chat-new" class="chat-new">{{ t("chat.page.new", "New") }}</button>
      {#- On a phone the list is not in the flow — it stood under the whole thread and
          the box, past everything — but behind this: the page's one overlay, a sheet
          (2026-09-10, targum-internal#238). Drawn only at phone width; the stylesheet
          decides. -#}
      <button type="button" id="chat-open-list" class="chat-open-list"
              aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="chat-list">{{ t("chat.page.conversations", "Conversations") }}</button>
    </div>
    {#- Newest first, each with when it was last opened; "More" at the foot for the next
        page. A row writes the conversation into the address, so a conversation can be
        linked to and the back button goes to the one before. -#}
    <ul class="chat-list" id="chat-list"></ul>
  </aside>

  {#- The page is the viewport since 2026-09-10 (targum-internal#247): the thread
      scrolls inside itself and the box stays in view at any length of conversation,
      where it used to sit under a thread of unbounded height and scroll away with it. -#}
  <section class="chat-thread" id="chat-thread" aria-live="polite">
    {#- The English under every Hebrew line is folded, and a tap on the pair opens it
        (2026-09-10, targum-internal#241): "I would just ignore the Hebrew and read the
        English." This opens all of it at once, and is remembered. Hidden until there
        is a pair to open, and for a reader with no known words, who sees it all open. -#}
    <button type="button" class="chat-english" id="chat-english" aria-pressed="false" hidden>{{ t("chat.page.show-translations", "Show translations") }}</button>
    {#- What this is, said once to a reader with no conversations yet. The copy is the
        product's register: precise, unpatronising, no selling. -#}
    <p class="chat-empty" id="chat-empty">{{ t("chat.page.ask-us-for-something-to-read-or", "Ask us for something to read, or ask what you know.
      We answer from the library and your own shelf.") }}</p>
    {% include '_chips.html.j2' %}
  {% include '_first_language.html.j2' %}
    <ol class="turns" id="turns"></ol>
  </section>

  {#- The box, shared with the front door (`_composer.html.j2`). One conversation,
      always in Hebrew, graded to the reader's own words, with the English under every
      line — whatever language they write in. -#}
  {#- The month's hours, above the box and only when they matter: past three quarters
      used, so the cap is not the first anybody hears of it, and never before — the whole
      count is on Your Progress, and a line in every reader's face on every visit was the
      metric "right in your face" (2026-09-10, targum-internal#237). Conversation comes
      out of the same hours a recording does. -#}
  <p class="chat-hours" id="chat-hours" hidden></p>
  {#- Where the reader is, when this is the drawer in a reader (2026-09-11): the sentence
      in front of them, and one press to ask about it. Every line typed here rides with
      it, so the answer is about the text. -#}
  <p class="chat-reading" id="chat-reading" hidden>
    <span class="chat-reading-label">{{ t("chat.page.reading", "Reading") }}</span>
    <bdi class="chat-reading-text" id="chat-reading-text" dir="auto"></bdi>
    <button type="button" class="chat-reading-ask" id="chat-reading-ask">{{ t("chat.page.explain-this-sentence", "Explain this sentence") }}</button>
  </p>
  {% set placeholder = t("chat.page.write-in-hebrew-or-english", "Write in Hebrew or English") %}
  {% include '_composer.html.j2' %}
</main>
{% if not embed %}{% include '_foot.html.j2' %}{% endif %}
<script>
window.TARGUM_KEY = "{{ token }}";
window.TARGUM_INTO = {{ into|tojson }};
window.TARGUM_LANGUAGES = { {% for code, name in languages %}"{{ code }}": "{{ name }}"{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %} };
{% if strings %}window.TARGUM_STRINGS = {{ strings|tojson }};
{% endif %}</script>
<script>{{ asset('strings.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('lang.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('sync.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('account.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('bring.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('chips.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('first.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('speak.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('claim.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('chat.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
